<section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">

<div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Metal stud partitioning offers straight, fire-resistant, and lightweight wall framing for offices, retail, and homes across Edinburgh. CSCS-accredited installation with Scottish Building Standards compliance and 12-month guarantee.</p>
</div>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Metal Stud Partitioning Service</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Metal stud partitioning has become the preferred choice for modern construction and refurbishment projects across Edinburgh. Unlike traditional timber framing, metal studs are straight, dimensionally stable, and resistant to warping, rot, and pests. At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we specialise in metal stud partition systems that deliver speed, strength, and flexibility for both commercial and residential clients throughout the capital and the Lothians.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh's dynamic property market — from New Town and Stockbridge office conversions to Leith Waterfront commercial fit-outs, Bruntsfield residential renovations, and Portobello retail units — creates consistent demand for professional metal stud partitioning. Our CSCS-accredited team delivers partition walls that meet Scottish Building Standards Part A structural requirements and Part B fire safety regulations, ensuring every installation is safe, compliant, and built to last.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Metal C-stud and U-track framing systems (50mm, 70mm, 92mm, 146mm profiles)</li>
  <li>Single and double-layer plasterboard cladding</li>
  <li>Acoustic insulation for sound-rated partitions</li>
  <li>Fire-rated partitions (30-120 minutes)</li>
  <li>Integrated door frames and glazing apertures</li>
  <li>Demountable and relocatable partition options</li>
  <li>Corner bead and trim finishing</li>
  <li>Professional taping and jointing for seamless surfaces</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Metal Stud Partitioning?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Consistently straight and level walls:</strong> Metal studs do not warp, twist, or bow over time, ensuring your walls remain perfectly straight in Edinburgh's historic and modern buildings alike.</li>
  <li><strong>Fire-resistant and non-combustible:</strong> Steel framing adds fire safety to your building and meets Part B Scottish Building Standards when combined with fire-rated boards from British Gypsum or Knauf.</li>
  <li><strong>No warping, shrinking, or rot:</strong> Unlike timber, metal studs are unaffected by moisture, temperature changes, and pests — particularly important for Edinburgh's older properties with solid stone walls.</li>
  <li><strong>Lightweight and easy to handle:</strong> Metal studs are lighter than timber, making them faster to install and reducing structural load on older Edinburgh buildings where load-bearing capacity is a concern.</li>
  <li><strong>Ideal for large-scale commercial fit-outs:</strong> Metal stud partitioning is the industry standard for Edinburgh's growing commercial property sector, including office refurbs on St Andrew Square and retail fit-outs on Princes Street.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials & Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use industry-leading products from trusted manufacturers to ensure your metal stud partitions are strong, compliant, and built to last across Edinburgh's diverse property portfolio.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Galvanised steel C-studs and U-tracks (50mm, 70mm, 92mm, and 146mm profiles)</li>
  <li>British Gypsum Gyproc plasterboard (standard, moisture-resistant, fire-rated, soundbloc)</li>
  <li>Knauf plasterboard and metal framing systems</li>
  <li>Rockwool and Isover acoustic insulation batts</li>
  <li>Fire-rated intumescent sealants and cavity barriers</li>
  <li>Steel corner beads and edge trim</li>
  <li>Joint compound and paper tape for seamless finishing</li>
  <li>Celotex and Kingspan insulated plasterboard for thermal upgrades</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Applications & Use Cases</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Metal stud partitioning is suitable for a wide range of building types and project sizes across Edinburgh.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Office fit-outs and open-plan reconfigurations in the New Town and Stockbridge</li>
  <li>Retail store fitting and display wall construction on Princes Street and St James Centre</li>
  <li>Healthcare facility partition systems for NHS Lothian and private clinics</li>
  <li>School and education building interiors across Edinburgh Council areas</li>
  <li>Residential extensions and loft conversions in Morningside, Bruntsfield, and Marchmont</li>
  <li>Industrial unit and warehouse partitioning in Leith and Portobello</li>
  <li>Hotels and hospitality refurbishment in the Old Town and West End</li>
  <li>Student accommodation and HMO conversions across the city</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">How It Works</h2>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Free Quote:</strong> Call or fill in our form. We will assess your layout, load-bearing requirements, and any acoustic or fire-rating needs across your Edinburgh property.</li>
  <li><strong>Detailed Plan:</strong> We confirm stud sizes, board types, insulation, and finishing specifications. Everything is agreed upfront with no hidden extras — including Scottish Building Standards compliance documentation.</li>
  <li><strong>Professional Installation:</strong> Our CSCS-registered team installs the metal stud framework, fixes plasterboard to both sides, and completes joints with professional taping and finishing.</li>
  <li><strong>Quality Check & Handover:</strong> We inspect every wall for straightness and finish quality, provide full compliance documentation, and leave your site clean and ready for decoration.</li>
</ol>

